                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/291</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Yokohama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Scidmore</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-19T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>Your February 10. Your plan approved. Felton is arranging to cable $75,000 additional to $50,000 sent
                    to Emerson last week. For your
                    confidential information, amount of Russian funds available has proved very much
                    less than $1,500,000 originally allocated. However, there appears to be
                    sufficient for three or four months longer, by which time situation may have
                    altered for the better sufficiently to release additional funds. In any event,
                    you can rely upon Department’s guaranteeing salaries, so long as service lasts,
                    and transportation and salaries for safe return to this country. Before you
                    return with the men, please confer with American Ambassador at Tokyo, whom
                    Department is instructing to advise you fully regarding the friendly attitude
                    toward Russia which has been manifested consistently by this Government.
                    Department congratulates you on difficulties you have overcome. Notify
                    Ambassador at Petrograd when you arrive at Harbin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
